   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p>The image shows how the complement system can bind to and destroys a pathogen.</p>\n<p>Suppose a genetic mutation prevented C2 and C4 proteins from being built properly. Would the entire complement system be compromised? Why or why not?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 758789,
     "content_html": "No, because the complement system functions as a cascade, with each protein triggering the activity of the next protein in the cascade."
    },
    {
     "id": 758790,
     "content_html": "Yes, because the complement system functions as a cascade, with each protein triggering the activity of the next protein in the cascade."
    },
    {
     "id": 758788,
     "content_html": "Yes, because all the proteins of the complement system function independently."
    },
    {
     "id": 758787,
     "content_html": "No, because all the proteins of the complement system function independently."
    }
